Test session key update request from client to server

Pre-test Settings:
- in order to decode communication in Wireshark set:
  Edit -> Preferences -> Protocols -> TLS -> (Pre)-Master-Secret log filename
  to /tmp/sslkeys.log

Security events:
- notice: TLS handshake successfully performed

Expected:
- After successful handshake, KeyUpdate message (visible in Wireshark, if
  decoded) with `update_requested (1)` flag is sent from client by entering `K`
  in the console.

  Server should respond with KeyUpdate message in order to force client to
  update its key material (check using Wireshark).
